<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/6th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Pallene</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 546 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pallene">Pallene</a> was fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attica">Attica</a> around 546 BCE, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peisistratus">Peisistratus</a>, returning from exile with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> and allies, surprised and routed the Athenian forces near the sanctuary of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athena">Athena</a> at Pallene. The victory gave him his third and lasting tyranny over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>, which he passed on to his sons Hippias and Hipparchus.</p></div>
